<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head>
  <title>About the Bell</title>
  
  <%- include("partials/metadata") %>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css"></head> <body>
  <%- include("partials/header") %>


<main>
  <section class="about-section">
    <div class="about-inner">
      <h1 class="about-title order-title">Campana Sonat Omnibus</h1>

      <hr class="order-rule">

      <p class="about-text">
        The Bell is the central symbol of the Order of the Lion's Bell. Throughout history, bells have marked moments of awakening: calling communities to gather, announcing the passage of time, and reminding humanity of mortality. In the philosophy of the Order, the Bell represents the moment in which truth becomes clear to the listener.
      </p>

        <div class="divider-symbol">✶✶</div>

      <p class="about-text">
        The Bell rings for all. Its call is not limited to a particular people, tradition, or belief. The sound of the Bell symbolizes the universal possibility of awakening. Every human being lives within reach of the same call toward knowledge, understanding, and truth.
      </p>

      <div class="divider-symbol">✶✶</div>

      <p class="about-text">
        To hear the Bell is to recognize the presence of truth within the world and within oneself. Not all who hear the Bell understand its meaning, and not all who understand its meaning answer its call. Those who choose to follow the call begin the path of the Akousmatikoi.
      </p>


      <div class="divider-symbol">✶✶</div>

      <p class="about-text">
        Within the Order, those who continue along the path of knowledge eventually become Heralds of the Lion, learning the truth and the deeper meanings of the Bell.
      </p>


      <div class="divider-symbol">✶✶</div>

      <p class="about-text">
        The ringing of a bell also reminds us of the passage of time. Every moment carries the possibility of awakening, yet time is finite. The Bell therefore symbolizes both opportunity and urgency.
      </p>


      <div class="divider-symbol">✶✶</div>

      <p class="about-quote">
        ὁ ἔχων ὦτα ἀκούειν ἀκουέτω<br>
        <span>"He who has ears to hear, let him hear."</span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>










